=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: r1
diagnosis_text:
The border router r1 has a complete and correct FRR configuration file at `/etc/frr/frr.conf` — it declares OSPF router-id 10.0.0.76, announces its two core-facing point-to-point links (10.0.0.32/30 to csw1 and 10.0.0.36/30 to csw2) into area 0, and includes `default-information originate` to redistribute its ISP-derived default route (via 203.0.113.1) into the OSPF domain. However, the FRR package is not installed on r1: `zebra` and `ospfd` binaries are absent, there is no FRR entry in the runit service directory (`/etc/sv/` contains only dnsmasq and ssh), and no FRR process is running. As a result, r1 never forms an OSPF adjacency — confirmed by csw1's neighbor table showing only five neighbors (csw2, dswa1, dswa2, dswb1, dswb2) with r1 conspicuously missing. The OSPF domain contains zero external LSAs, meaning no default route (0.0.0.0/0) is distributed to any switch. All gateway routers (dswa1, dswa2, dswb1, dswb2) and core switches (csw1, csw2) have complete internal routing for 10.1–10.6 subnets, so inter-office traffic between PC1 (10.1.0.100) and srv1 (10.5.0.4) works correctly — the reported inter-office failure is a misidentification of the symptom. The actual failure is internet connectivity: dswa1 (10.1.0.2) returns ICMP Network Unreachable for any internet-bound packet. Root cause: FRR is not installed on r1, preventing OSPF participation and default-route injection. Fix: install FRR on r1 (`apt-get install frr`), enable ospfd and zebra daemons in `/etc/frr/daemons`, and start the service — the existing configuration is already correct.
=== END ===